components.responsibility:
Four rules, each with an xUnit twin in ArchitectureRulesTests and plants in eng/rules-harness/plants.json (one line that must fire, one correct line that must not):
- the store is spelled in one file;
- the workaround is switched in one place;
- PoolWatch never elevates;
- PoolWatch prints no verdict.

Patterns start with a literal (?m) and use a scoped (?i:...) where needed, as rules-parity requires. The RuleCases pins Q-085 names (C-001 counts, C-003, C-004, C-005, C-007, C-008, SettledCountProbe) are updated in the same change.

Built new and lean. It runs unelevated and uses NtQuerySystemInformation(22) plus GetPerformanceInfo through Add-Type, compatible with PowerShell 5.1 and 7.

-Prepare:
- publishes the exe through eng/dotnet.ps1 and builds the hook;
- writes prepare.json with an Rpre reading;
- records the environment: OS build, boot time, wcifs.sys version, Win32_SystemDriver state of wcifs/bindflt/CldFlt/WdFilter, SecurityCenter2 antivirus, whether OneDrive is running, and an optional fltmc paste. The paste counts only with the 'Filter Name ... Num Instances' header; otherwise the record says FILTERS UNDECIDED (R2-N3).

-Protocol:
- refuses to start when prepare.json, the exe or the hook is missing, or when boot age at R0 is over 30 min (X4);
- writes a plan line listing the expected arms in order, then R0;
- runs I0 (a 20-min raw idle window), 5 exe-full arms, 5 exe-cancel/close arms (4 cancels and 1 close, using the hook's existing triggers), then I1;
- takes /before, /exit and /settled (+10 min) marks per arm. Each mark holds pool bytes, Available MB, per-tag allocs/frees/bytes as an array (WC*, FMwi, FMfc, FMfn, File, NtfF, Toke), the System handle count and its 0x120089 count;
- writes each arm line with exitCode, report status, notScanned, opensUnderExcludedStore, the hook's acted line and foldersAtCancel, guardStop and guardAtStart;
- applies a machine guard per arm: combined pool growth over that arm's /before above 2 GiB, or Available below 3 GiB, kills FsAnalyser.exe and records guardStop.

-Rehearse runs the same code over a generated %TEMP% tree (about 2,000 folders and 10,000 files), with 60 s / 30 s windows and folder-count triggers, and skips the boot-age check. Every line is tagged rehearsal:true, and the scratch is deleted in finally unless -Keep is passed.

There is no settle gate, drift judgement, pressure step, tolerance, ScanArm, L/S/P arm, dir arm or store-size walk.

contracts.error_cases:
RUN INCOMPLETE names each of these:
- an arm in the plan but not in arms.jsonl;
- a /before, /exit or /settled mark missing;
- any needed field null (m7);
- any guardStop; arms with guardAtStart are listed as 'not measured: guard already exceeded at start (cascade from <arm>)';
- not exactly 5 exe-full and 5 exe-cancel/close arms;
- an exe-full with exit not 0, no report, status not Completed, or (real mode only) notScanned < 1 or opensUnderExcludedStore not 0;
- an exe-cancel or exe-close with no '^acted ' line or no foldersAtCancel (StartupHook.cs:653 and :665 refused lines count as not acted);
- an exe-cancel whose status is not Cancelled.
